    "type": "question",
    "label": "5",
    "prompt": "Ten $\\text{cm}^3$ of silver and $5\\text{ cm}^3$ of copper weigh $150\\text{ g}$. One cubic centimetre of silver weighs $1\\frac{1}{6}$ times as much as $1\\text{ cm}^3$ of copper. Find the weight of $1\\text{ cm}^3$ of each of the metals.",
